+++ b/.changeset/preencoded-keyframe-pacing.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+---
+webrtc-sys: patch
+---
+
+Enable WebRTC keyframe queue flushing in the zero-playout-delay factory. When the first packet
+of a new keyframe arrives, superseded queued packets for that video stream and
+its RTX stream are removed unless another keyframe is still being paced.
+Audio and unrelated streams retain their queues. This bounds recovery work
+without dropping arbitrary encoded references, changing capture cadence, or
+replacing an encoder or publication.
